      <Class TestSplit>
        <Function test_chapters_are_found_by_heading_with_no_printed_page_footer>
          FY2023/24 executives: the first chapter page carries no printed
          '1', so find_offset returned None and the old walk extracted nothing
          from a 555-page volume.
        <Function test_the_heading_form_without_of>
        <Function test_a_heading_naming_a_different_county_is_refused>
          'COUNTY EXECUTIVE OF KILIFI – NO.2' where the contents say No.2 is
          Kwale: file it under neither.
        <Function test_a_contents_entry_with_no_chapter_is_reported>
        <Function test_the_last_chapter_stops_at_the_appendix>
      <Class TestSegment>
        <Function test_paragraph_numbers_past_999>
          FY2024/25 executives numbers paragraphs continuously to 1323. The
          3-digit pattern merged every finding from 1000 on into the one before.
        <Function test_an_appendix_citation_inside_a_finding_does_not_end_the_chapter>
          'Appendix VI to the financial statements on summary of fixed assets
          register reflects...' starts a line in chapter 36. The national rule
          broke the chapter there and lost 40 findings.
        <Function test_a_number_oag_skipped_does_not_lose_the_rest_of_the_chapter>
          1266 appears nowhere in the FY2024/25 executives volume. With a
          strict prev+1 rule, 1267-1282 were all lost.
        <Function test_a_year_at_the_start_of_a_wrapped_line_is_not_a_finding>
        <Function test_a_numbered_list_inside_a_finding_is_not_a_finding>
          A prior-year issues table inside the chapter numbers from 1.
        <Function test_a_prior_year_issues_table_is_not_findings>
          FY2024/25 assemblies, Mombasa, p.14, verbatim. Finding 2 lists last
          year's six issues as a numbered table. With prev=2, table rows 3-6
          passed as four body-less findings, and the real 3 and 4 after them
          then read as going backwards and were dropped.
        <Function test_a_table_row_that_wraps_does_not_end_the_table>
        <Function test_a_table_is_ended_by_a_number_that_breaks_its_sequence>
          No heading after the table: the next real finding (prev+1 = 841)
          is not 7, so the table is over.
        <Function test_the_chapter_heading_is_not_recorded_as_a_sub_section>
        <Function test_the_national_walk_stops_only_at_an_appendix_heading>
          The national default keeps ``stop_at_appendix``, which the county
          volumes turn off, but only the end matter's HEADING ends a chapter.
          A finding that opens a line with "Appendix A ..." does not (six such
          lines in the FY2024/25 national book each cut a chapter short). A
          number that does not continue the sequence is still body text.
